/*
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * AMIGO HOSPITAL ROBOT - NodeMCU (ESP8266) RFID Reader & Supabase Integration
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * Hardware Wiring (NodeMCU ESP8266 <-> MFRC522 RFID Reader):
 *   - MFRC522 SDA (SS)  -> NodeMCU Pin D8 (GPIO15)
 *   - MFRC522 SCK       -> NodeMCU Pin D5 (GPIO14)
 *   - MFRC522 MOSI      -> NodeMCU Pin D7 (GPIO13)
 *   - MFRC522 MISO      -> NodeMCU Pin D6 (GPIO12)
 *   - MFRC522 RST       -> NodeMCU Pin D3 (GPIO0)
 *   - MFRC522 GND       -> GND
 *   - MFRC522 3.3V      -> 3.3V (DO NOT CONNECT TO 5V!)
 *
 * Optional Feedback Hardware:
 *   - Buzzer / LED      -> NodeMCU Pin D1 (GPIO5)
 *   - Status LED        -> NodeMCU Pin D2 (GPIO4)
 *
 * Dependencies (Install via Arduino Library Manager):
 *   - MFRC522 by githubmonk / miguelbalboa
 *   - ArduinoJson by Benoit Blanchon (v6.x)
 *   - ESP8266WiFi & ESP8266HTTPClient (Built into ESP8266 Board Core)
 *
 * Supabase Table SQL Setup (Run in Supabase SQL Editor if table doesn't exist):
 *   CREATE TABLE rfid_scans (
 *       id BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
 *       rfid_tag VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
 *       robot_id INT DEFAULT 1,
 *       status VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'scanned',
 *       scanned_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT now()
 *   );
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */

